Rule 1 (x and y must have the same type)
{x: tensor, y: tensor} |= dtype_(x) = dtype_(y)
>>
Rule 2 (x must have a valid dtype)
{x: tensor} |= (dtype_(x) = 7) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 8) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 3) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 6) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 2) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 1) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 4) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 9) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 10) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 12)
>>
Rule 5 (x and y must have compatible shapes for broadcasting - stricter)
{x: tensor, y: tensor} |= (ndim(x) = 0) ∨ (ndim(y) = 0) ∨ (ndim(x) = ndim(y) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(x) - 1] : (shape(x, i) = shape(y, i) ∨ shape(x, i) = 1 ∨ shape(y, i) = 1))
>>
Rule 7 (at least one tensor must have more than 0 elements)
{x: tensor, y: tensor} |= (shape(x, 0) * shape(y, 0) > 0) ∨ (ndim(x) = 0) ∨ (ndim(y) = 0)
>>
Rule 8 (at least one tensor must have positive shape)
{x: tensor, y: tensor} |= (ndim(x) = 0) ∨ (ndim(y) = 0) ∨ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(x) - 1] : shape(x, i) > 0) ∨ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(y) - 1] : shape(y, i) > 0)
>>
Rule 9 (if one tensor is a scalar, then the other must be a valid tensor)
{x: tensor, y: tensor} |= if ndim(x) = 0 then (dtype_(y) = 7) ∨ (dtype_(y) = 8) ∨ (dtype_(y) = 3) ∨ (dtype_(y) = 6) ∨ (dtype_(y) = 2) ∨ (dtype_(y) = 1) ∨ (dtype_(y) = 4) ∨ (dtype_(y) = 9) ∨ (dtype_(y) = 10) ∨ (dtype_(y) = 12) else if ndim(y) = 0 then (dtype_(x) = 7) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 8) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 3) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 6) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 2) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 1) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 4) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 9) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 10) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 12)
>>
Rule 10 (if x is a scalar, y must also be a scalar, or vice-versa)
{x: tensor, y: tensor} |= (ndim(x) = 0 ∧ ndim(y) = 0) ∨ (ndim(x) > 0) ∨ (ndim(y) > 0)
>>
Rule 11 (x and y must be of the same rank, or at least one must be scalar)
{x: tensor, y: tensor} |= (ndim(x) = ndim(y)) ∨ (ndim(x) = 0) ∨ (ndim(y) = 0)
>>
Rule 41 (Check broadcasting requirements using if/then/else)
{x: tensor, y: tensor} |= if ndim(x) = 0 then true else if ndim(y) = 0 then true else if ndim(x) ≠ ndim(y) then false else if ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(x) - 1] : shape(x, i) = shape(y, i) ∨ shape(x, i) = 1 ∨ shape(y, i) = 1 then true else false
